esources\":[]}},{\"resourceOfId\":\"workshop-op7ym\",\"resourceId\":\"lesson-c3344\",\"position\":5,\"metadata\":{\"tier\":\"standard\"},\"organizationId\":null,\"createdAt\":\"2025-05-01T09:12:14.551Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2025-05-01T09:12:14.551Z\",\"deletedAt\":null,\"resource\":{\"id\":\"lesson-c3344\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"fields\":{\"title\":\"Showing Tool Calls In The Frontend\",\"slug\":\"showing-tool-calls-in-the-frontend~l68vq\",\"state\":\"draft\",\"visibility\":\"unlisted\"},\"resources\":[]}},{\"resourceOfId\":\"workshop-op7ym\",\"resourceId\":\"lesson-p85ck\",\"position\":6,\"metadata\":{\"tier\":\"standard\"},\"organizationId\":null,\"createdAt\":\"2025-05-30T18:41:14.482Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2025-05-30T18:41:14.482Z\",\"deletedAt\":null,\"resource\":{\"id\":\"lesson-p85ck\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"fields\":{\"title\":\"Search Grounding (optional)\",\"slug\":\"search-grounding-optional~p85ck\",\"state\":\"draft\",\"visibility\":\"unlisted\"},\"resources\":[]}},{\"resourceOfId\":\"workshop-op7ym\",\"resourceId\":\"lesson-t0g70\",\"position\":7,\"metadata\":{\"tier\":\"standard\"},\"organizationId\":null,\"createdAt\":\"2025-05-30T18:40:53.621Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2025-05-30T18:40:53.621Z\",\"deletedAt\":null,\"resource\":{\"id\":\"lesson-t0g70\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"fields\":{\"title\":\"Rate Limiting (optional)\",\"slug\":\"rate-limiting-optional~t0g70\",\"state\":\"draft\",\"visibility\":\"unlisted\"},\"resources\":[]}},{\"resourceOfId\":\"workshop-op7ym\",\"resourceId\":\"lesson-vc3fs\",\"position\":8,\"metadata\":{\"tier\":\"standard\"},\"organizationId\":null,\"createdAt\":\"2025-06-03T18:29:51.812Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2025-06-03T18:29:51.812Z\",\"deletedAt\":null,\"resource\":{\"id\":\"lesson-vc3fs\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"fields\":{\"title\":\"Rate Limiting Anonymous Users (optional)\",\"slug\":\"rate-limiting-anonymous-users-optional~u855m\",\"state\":\"draft\",\"visibility\":\"unlisted\"},\"resources\":[]}},{\"resourceOfId\":\"workshop-op7ym\",\"resourceId\":\"lesson-sjetv\",\"position\":9,\"metadata\":{\"tier\":\"standard\"},\"organizationId\":null,\"createdAt\":\"2025-07-14T12:52:48.673Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2025-07-14T12:52:48.673Z\",\"deletedAt\":null,\"resource\":{\"id\":\"lesson-sjetv\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"fields\":{\"title\":\"Connecting Our App To MCP Servers (optional)\",\"slug\":\"connecting-our-app-to-mcp-servers-optional-sjetv\",\"state\":\"draft\",\"visibility\":\"unlisted\"},\"resources\":[]}}]}}]}]}]}]]}]}]}]}]\n64:T59c,Using `useChat` from Vercel AI SDK makes it easy to get a basic chatbot up and running. But turning that quick prototype into a fully functional, persistent chat product is where most developers get stuck.\n\nHow do you save user and assistant messages as they stream in? What’s the right moment to create and store a new chat ID? How do you support routing by `chatId` and keep your UI in sync when the chat history changes?\n\nThis workshop is all about bridging that gap—taking your chat from demo to durable, with backend persistence, real-time updates, and solid routing.\n\nYou will:\n\n- Build a` POST /api/chat` endpoint using `createDataStreamResponse` to stream completions from OpenAI\n- Use Drizzle to create a new chat record and return the generated `chatId` over the stream itself\n- Automatically redirect users to the new `/chat/:chatId` route once it’s available\n- Save each user and assistant message to your database as it streams in\n- Rehydrate the chat UI with existing messages pulled from the database when loading a past conversation\n-   Keep your sidebar list of chats updated using route revalidation, so it always reflects the latest state\n\nBy the end of this workshop, you’ll have a end-to-end persistent chat experience—streaming, saving, routing, and reloading conversations seamlessly. More importantly, you’ll know how to build chat apps that feel real and resilient, not just impressive prototypes.\n\n52:[\"$\",\"li\",\"workshop-9f7e9\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L47\",null